# Canonical board-game admissions and audit decisions are owned by T's
# authenticated repository account. GitHub cannot distinguish two Hermes
# personas that use this same account, so CI enforces three protected-branch
# transitions: scout packet, audit-only decision, then deterministic promotion.
# This is a single-account repository: GitHub forbids approving your own PR,
# so required approving reviews stay at zero by design and this file cannot
# gate merges. It documents ownership; the human key is T's authenticated
# account merging each PR behind the required green `validate` check.
